// Title: Staging paths, svchost without -k, unlinked processes
// Severity: High
// Why: Malware runs from user-writable folders (Temp, AppData, Users\Public, ProgramData, PerfLogs, Recycle Bin, Windows\Tasks, spool\drivers\color ...). Every genuine svchost has "-k <group>". A running process that psscan finds but pslist does not was unlinked from the active process list (DKOM rootkit).
// FalsePositives: Per-user apps (Teams, OneDrive, Zoom) and installers legitimately run from AppData/Temp (Medium). psscan also finds processes from before a reboot; those are filtered by boot time.
// MITRE: T1036.005, T1014
// Refs: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_execution_path.yml ; https://github.com/volatilityfoundation/volatility/wiki/Command-Reference-Mal
Det_ProcessLocation()
| extend SeverityRank = SevRank(Severity)
| order by SeverityRank desc
| project-away SeverityRank
